  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nIn one operation, Chef can choose any subsequence of the array and any integer XXX and then add XXX to **all** the elements of the chosen subsequence.\n\nDetermine the **minimum** number of operations required to make all the elements of the array **distinct**.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of Array AAA.\nNext line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,A3,…,ANA_1, A_2, A_3, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,A3​,…,AN​ - denoting the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **minimum** number of operations required to make all the elements distinct.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤40001 \\leq T \\leq 40001≤T≤4000",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases do not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n3 3 3\n6\n1 3 2 1 2 2\n4\n1 2 1 2\n5\n1 3 2 4 6",
        "output": "2\n2\n1\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\nOperation 111: Choose the subsequence {A1}\\{A_1\\}{A1​} and add X=1X = 1X=1 to the elements. The array becomes A=[4,3,3]A = [4, 3, 3]A=[4,3,3].\nOperation 222: Choose the subsequence {A2}\\{A_2\\}{A2​} and add X=2X = 2X=2 to the elements. The array becomes A=[4,5,3]A = [4, 5, 3]A=[4,5,3].\n\nThus, we require, minimum 222 operations to make all the elements distinct.\nTest case 222:\n\nOperation 111: Choose the subsequence {A1,A6}\\{A_1, A_6\\}{A1​,A6​} and add X=4X = 4X=4 to the elements. The array becomes A=[5,3,2,1,2,6]A = [5, 3, 2, 1, 2, 6]A=[5,3,2,1,2,6].\nOperation 222: Choose the subsequence {A3}\\{A_3\\}{A3​} and add X=5X = 5X=5 to the elements. The array becomes A=[5,3,7,1,2,6]A = [5, 3, 7, 1, 2, 6]A=[5,3,7,1,2,6].\n\nThus, we require, minimum 222 operations to make all the elements distinct.\nTest case 333:\n\nOperation 111: Choose the subsequence {A3,A4}\\{A_3, A_4\\}{A3​,A4​} and add X=2X = 2X=2 to the elements. The array becomes A=[1,2,3,4]A = [1, 2, 3, 4]A=[1,2,3,4].\n\nThus, we require, minimum 111 operation to make all the elements distinct.\nTest case 444: All the elements are distinct. We need zero operations."
      }
    ]
  },
